      "content": "it's interesting you bring up the idea of \"heightened perceptive/learning capability.\" i mean, if we look at transhumanism or the concept of evolutionary leaps, isn't it possible that what you're calling \"highly variable\" is actually just the early stages of a divergent phenotype? like, if someone is showing measurable, sustained increases in processing speed and metabolic efficiency (like the sleep thing), wouldn't it be logical to classify that as a transition toward a more optimized human model rather than just a \"variation\"?",
